# The spill tier counts what its restores saved (`saved_s`, `saved_tokens`, `unpriced`). A restore saves the prefill of
# the tokens the GPU no longer held: the stored point's length less the longest state the GPU still had, which prestage
# already finds before it reads the disk past it (`held`, rank 0). Each restore is priced once, when it happens, at the
# engine's own prefill speed less the restore's load time, so the counter only grows. The speed is /health's: its last
# 32 finished requests with at least 1,024 uncached tokens (`prefill_price_tps`, the board's real-prompt filter); with
# none yet, the restore is counted unpriced. The board priced every restored token at one fixed speed, which overstated
# a restore whose prefix the GPU still held (2026-10-16).

